repository: 'https://github.com/kima-org/kima'
abstract: >-
  We present a new method to determine the posterior
  distribution for the planet occurrence rate from
  radial-velocity (RV) observations. The approach combines
  results from the analysis of individual RV datasets of
  several stars, using importance sampling to reweight the
  posterior samples. This bypasses the calculation of
  detection limits with injection-recovery and does not
  require the explicit definition of a detection threshold.
  We demonstrate the method on simulated RV datasets,
  showing that it recovers unbiased estimates of the
  occurrence rate in different regions, with increasing
  precision as more stars are included in the analysis.
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - radial velocities
